tainer class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"188\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D466 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> is the following:</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-q-119300-e-0\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-119300-e-0\"></div>  \n\n<p>To see this more clearly, notice that if we draw a horizontal line, the slopes touching the line do not vary as we move left and right along the line.</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-q-119300-e-1\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-119300-e-1\"></div></div></div>",
